From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haoze <90812991+HaozeG@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:56:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] [G3.1] sdk: add flex_alloc_api.h from
 bowwang-dev/softhier-deeploy

Copied unchanged from soft_hier/flex_cluster_sdk/runtime/deeploy_include/flex_alloc_api.h
(branch bowwang-dev/softhier-deeploy, 99b60c3) into runtime/include/, which the SDK build
searches. softhier-mlir's runtime/sh_ops.c includes it; it declares flex_hbm_malloc and
flex_hbm_free, which flex_alloc.h of this branch already defines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../flex_cluster_sdk/runtime/include/flex_alloc_api.h  | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 soft_hier/flex_cluster_sdk/runtime/include/flex_alloc_api.h

diff --git a/soft_hier/flex_cluster_sdk/runtime/include/flex_alloc_api.h b/soft_hier/flex_cluster_sdk/runtime/include/flex_alloc_api.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1a14e24
--- /dev/null
+++ b/soft_hier/flex_cluster_sdk/runtime/include/flex_alloc_api.h
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+// flex_alloc_api.h
+#ifndef FLEX_ALLOC_API_H
+#define FLEX_ALLOC_API_H
+
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+void* flex_hbm_malloc(uint32_t size);
+void  flex_hbm_free(void* ptr);
+
+#endif
